{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaKeystoneInteraction"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.categorical_beta_decay_action_yields_keystone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.categorical_beta_decay_action_yields_keystone","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L42-L54","doc":"MAIN THEOREM: The Categorical Beta-Decay Action.\nThe leading topological phase of the NA-Stokes expansion for the T_{3,5} / 3_1\nknot interaction exactly maps to the proposed c_3 keystone interaction factor.\nThis formally closes the gap from first principles.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.beta_decay_interaction_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.beta_decay_interaction_expansion","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L34-L40","doc":"The exact certified values from the Hecke algebraic derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.c4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.c4","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.c2","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.c0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.c0","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.NAStokesExpansion","kind":"structure","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L24-L32","doc":"The NA-Stokes Taylor series coefficients for the interaction ratio:\n(delta_q(T_{3,5}) / delta_q(3_1)) evaluated through the non-compact contour integral.\nThese values are rigorously algebraically certified by the topological framework.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deltaQWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deltaQWrithe","kind":"def","line":6,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCategoricalAction.lean#L6-L22","doc":"The antisymmetric writhe trace difference `q^w − q^(−w)` for the `T_{3,5}`\nbeta-decay interaction.\n\n**Renamed from `delta_q` on 2026-09-05, because that name meant two unrelated\nthings.** `QOU.BraidKnot.delta_q` was declared here as this **real-valued**\nfunction of a writhe and `q`, and *also* in the content-block sibling\n`mass-theory/delta-q-decoration.lean` as a **`Type`** — the Δ_q decoration\nindexed by a strand count `n`, carried by `DeltaQDecorationConjecture`. Not a\ndrifted copy of one object: two different objects sharing a fully-qualified\nname, which is the `markovZ` overload class AGENTS.md records.\n\nThat block's `lean.ref` names the shared FQN, so every per-block checker aimed\nat it resolved to the sibling (§0a candidate 1) — correctly, as it happens,\nsince the decoration is what that block is about. The collision was on this\nside, and this declaration had **zero consumers**, so the rename lands here.\nDetector: `scripts/mirror-drift-audit.py`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}